def reverse-pmos
  title "Reverse-polarity protection with a P-MOSFET"
  about "AO3401A in the supply path: drain at the input, source at the output, gate to ground through 10 kΩ. It
      conducts with milliohms instead of a diode drop; with a reversed source the gate is above the source and the
      body diode blocks. For inputs up to about 10 V (VGS max ±12 V)."
  port in "the supply from the connector"
  port out "the protected rail"
  port gnd "ground"
  part Q1 transistor AO3401A lcsc C15127 "{as}: reverse-polarity PMOS"
  part R1 resistor 0805W8F1002T5E lcsc C17414 value 10k "{as}: gate to ground 10 k"
  net in Q1.drain
  net out @in Q1.source
  net gate 0..100 mV Q1.gate R1.1
  net gnd R1.2
  covers LVL.undefined PATH.reverse
  notes "Graph: the connector that feeds 'in' gets \"source\": \"reversible\"."
  notes "Above about 10 V input: a zener (10 V) from gate to source and a larger gate resistor, so that VGS stays
      below 12 V."
  notes "AO3401A: 3.2 A at 70 °C, 60 mΩ at VGS -4.5 V; edakit sim checks current and power (LIM)."
